    {
        "text": "They will not admit that those who fall try to cling to the sunlight, but grasp only lightning.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "'The Mysterious Spectator'"
    },
    {
        "text": "Must they accept their fall?",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "'Molly'"
    },
    {
        "text": "They can choose to not look back at the peak.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "'The Mysterious Spectator'"
    },
    {
        "text": "If they would turn their gaze around, they would realize that it is no abyss lying before them, but fertile earth in which infinite possibilities lie.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "'The Mysterious Spectator'"
    },
    {
        "text": "You say the abyss can be conquered? You do not know the truth of the abyss, nor do you understand that time is short.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "'Molly'"
    },
    {
        "text": "The abyss lies before us. We can fill it with flesh, and burn the remnants with blood, leaving behind wide open fields for those who come after.",
        "tag": "name",
        "value": "'The Mysterious Spectator'"
    },
